        "reason": "Full Proposition3.1 wellposedness/stationarity is a real source consumer, not established by source baseline or a clock leaf.",
        "region_id": "algorithm-and-prop31",
        "source_URL": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
        "source_id": "S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
        "source_tag": "p",
        "text": "For every fixed $y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ and initial phase space point $(x_{0},p_{0})$ , the event-driven dynamics in Algorithm 1 , with the reference point fixed at $\\widetilde{x}$ , defines a unique non-explosive, time-homogeneous Markov process. The phase space measure $\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ is stationary for this process. In particular, the returned position $x_{\\pi}$ is well-defined almost surely.",
        "independent_review": "Accepted exact source-range classification within this bounded selected universe; implementation coverage follows its named node dispositions, not automatic theorem completion."
      },
